    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For q-77770, the transformation gives X=2x and Y=-x-3(4x+5)=-13x-15, hence 13X+2Y+30=0. For q-77653, X=-2x and Y=x+2(3-2x)=6-3x, hence 3X-2Y+12=0. Both ODEs have highest derivative order four. Graphs I and IV pass the horizontal line test; the nonzero-slope linear function is injective on all three intervals. The discontinuity graphs show the stated asymptotes, holes, and jumps. For q-104036, current option 2 depicts the same jump at x=-2 as the worked-solution image, despite different asset paths and endpoint colors. The Riemann sums use width 3/n, with left endpoints 3i/n and right endpoints 3k/n. Six points in general position determine C(6,2)=15 lines, and nine players play C(9,2)=36 games. For q-78131, the corner at zero is continuous, while the asymptote at -2 is not. For q-104051, f(5)=2, but the one-sided limits are 2 and 4, so only statements I and III are true. Finally, ln(A+1)=1 gives A=e-1.",
